+Target Gateway replay-domain preflight must resolve the non-secret `FIREMUD_GATEWAY_REPLAY_DOMAIN` value and require the exact versioned literal `gateway-connect-token-replay-v1`. It must also prove that every Gateway instance, the target Coordination Redis ACL/key helper, and migration/reset tooling resolve that same literal `{gateway-connect-token-replay-v1}` tag, then read back the readiness record plus bounded disposable replay/deny probe keys from the shared Coordination deployment and verify their common Cluster slot plus the readiness `replayAdmissionFence`. This is a cross-instance/continuity proof, not a host/port or configuration-presence check. The current preflight and Gateway helper do not implement this value, tagged-key readback, or replay-domain result; existing preflight passes remain partial non-authorizing evidence and player-facing admission stays quarantined.
